Cron jobs, explained on their own page
=====================================

The nav said "Schedules" and the page said "Schedules", so the feature was a word nobody could act on:
you open it and there is a list of things with clocks next to them, or nothing at all.

  * the page is titled "Cron jobs" and says what that means — a prompt that runs on a clock, five-field
    expression, this computer's time zone
  * the legend spells the five fields out with a worked example: `0 9 * * 1-5` is 09:00 Monday to Friday
  * each job shows its raw expression next to the friendly description, because the expression is the
    thing you actually came to check
  * an empty list now explains the idea and offers to create the first one, instead of rendering blank

The behaviour is unchanged — same runner, same approval rules. What changed is that the page stops
assuming you already know what it is.

